upstream commits and their authors; carry it in README.native-displayid,
and define what libdisplay-info3-native-hdr-api level 2 means.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 debian/README.native-displayid | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/README.native-displayid b/debian/README.native-displayid
index 46798d9..a8218aa 100644
--- a/debian/README.native-displayid
+++ b/debian/README.native-displayid
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ this bounded stack until separately tested. No Type 1/content metadata is
 fabricated, and native panel brightness is not mastering/content metadata.
 
 The source preserves the attributed historical CTA/lifecycle backports and
-local parser changes identified in the quilt header. The additive API derives
+local parser changes listed under "Attribution" below. The additive API derives
 from the locally reviewed, unpushed parser proposal 533a338, not an accepted
 upstream release. Human DCO, normative section verification, maintainer review
 and any public submission remain separate gates.
@@ -53,3 +53,41 @@ hardening and all ownership/failure assertions remain. Production keeps the
 distribution architecture's normal LTO policy (enabled on qualified amd64,
 not present in the qualified i386 distribution flags).
 The private observed panel capture is excluded from source/package payloads.
+
+API level
+---------
+
+libdisplay-info3 provides the virtual package libdisplay-info3-native-hdr-api
+at API level 2: the native DisplayID 2.x physical luminance getter
+(di_displayid2_data_block_get_luminance, added in hdr7) and the native
+chromaticity getter (di_displayid2_data_block_get_native_chromaticities, added
+in hdr8). Consumers of these private getters depend on the virtual package so
+that an archive libdisplay-info3 without them can never satisfy the
+dependency.
+
